          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong tripos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+hyperdoctrine"} first-order hyperdoctrine with equality
            satisfying an additional property that allows it to interpret
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+logic"} impredicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher-order+logic"} higher-order logic
            as well. In particular, every tripos gives rise to a corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %p
            The notion of tripos, due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Pitts"} Andrew Pitts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic toposes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability toposes
          %p
            The name ‘tripos’ is to be credited to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"} Peter Johnstone
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hyland"} Hyland
            work.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Recall that the data of a first-order hyperdoctrine
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} category of terms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Pred
                    %mi T
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi HeytAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pred_T: C_{T}^{op} \to HeytAlg
          %p
            to the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebras"} Heyting algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifiers"} quantifiers
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Pred
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pred_T(f)
            = succeed "." do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Pred
                    %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pred_T(f)
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            = succeed "." do
              %em pullback map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is a Heyting algebra, we let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|H|}
            denote the underlying set.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong tripos
              is a first-order hyperdoctrine
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              together with, for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P c
              and an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi in
                      %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Pred
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ×
                    %mi P
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in_c \in Pred_T(c \times P c)
              such that for any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              and element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Pred
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ×
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in Pred_T(c \times b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi b
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon b \to P c
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Pred
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi c
                      %mo ×
                      %mi χ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi in
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pred_T(1_c \times \chi)(in_c) = p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              need not be unique.)
          %p
            Another way of phrasing the definition is that to each object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
            there is an assigned object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(c)
            and an assigned
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi Pred
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, P c) \to {|Pred_T|}(c \times -)
          %p
            of set-valued functors; the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate"} predicate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi in
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in_c
            is the value of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_c
            under the assigned epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi Pred
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ×
                    %mi P
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(P c, P c) \to {|Pred_T(c \times P c)|}
            (
            %em à la
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          %p
            The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi in
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in_c
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em generic predicates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo =
                  %mi P
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = P 1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi in
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi in
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Pred
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} in = in_1 \in Pred_T(P)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi Pred
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, P) \to {|Pred_T|}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epis
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
